rocess) and differentia (keratin accumulation that gives cells their cornified character, as seen in nails, hair, and skin's outer layer), then working toward a fully vocalized final definition. I'm noticing a key distinction here—keratosis and keratinization are related but separate medical concepts, where keratosis describes a pathological skin condition while keratinization is the normal cellular process. Entry 743121 maps تقرن to \"keratosis\" with the definition \"كل نمو قرني مثل الثؤلول والجسأة,\" which represents a polysemy issue I need to flag in the YAML as contradicting evidence, since it's pointing to a different medical phenomenon than what the primary entry describes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5651,"cache_read_input_tokens":38394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5651},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1601022-f0a3-4249-b952-ea8c9e474690","uuid":"f50c1386-2500-4e97-b27f-2f9c25650eae"}
